  "summary": "I started my career as a Test Engineer working in manufacturing ensuring NCR's hardware products were tested within compliance. In the Test Engineer role, I've also managed the transition from in-house production to moving production to NCR's third-party suppliers. I took a two-year break from Engineering and went and became an Operations Program Manager managing the supply chain and ensuring Operations can produce Self-Serivce Checkout (SCO) machines, Optic Fuel Controllers, and NCR's Hardware servers for Hospitality and Retail businesses. Due to a shortage of manpower in the Global Test Engineering team, I was asked to come back to help fill a gap that was left when two colleagues left NCR for better opportunities. Present day I work on developing software for NPIs and support Operations Globally wherever NCR's products are built.",
